# RecipeManagerLegacy — Project Guide

Small command-line recipe manager in Python. This is the canonical project entry
point; tool-specific adapters (`.github/copilot-instructions.md`, etc.) point here
instead of copying these facts.

## Layout

- `src/recipe_manager/` — the package
  - `models.py` — `Ingredient` and `Recipe` dataclasses
  - `parsing.py`, `storage.py` — recipe text format and JSON load/save
  - `report.py`, `cli.py` — output and entry point
  - `analytics.py`, `catalog.py`, `meal_plans.py`, `pantry.py`, `shopping.py`,
    `exports.py` — feature modules
- `tests/` — pytest tests
- `data/` — sample recipes (`recipes.json`, `pancakes.txt`)
- `tools/` — MCP kitchen-service fixture

## Commands

```bash
uv sync --extra dev           # once: install with dev tooling
uv run tools/check.py         # the check: lint, type-check, tests
uv run pytest -q              # tests only, while iterating
```

Definition of done: `uv run tools/check.py` green, with its output in your report.
`uv run ruff format --check src tests` still flags a few legacy files — they get
formatted in a separate commit; until then, do not reformat files you were not asked
to change.

## Conventions

- Type hints on all public functions; docstrings on public APIs
- Prefer dataclasses over dicts; `pathlib` over `os.path`
- New behavior lands test-first: write the failing test, then implement
- Keep functions small; the legacy long functions are refactoring targets,
  not a style to imitate
